course: dictionary
lesson: 978
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Board is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use. «The teacher wrote the sum on the board» means a flat surface at the front of the class, not a long piece of wood.
explain: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer.» Squinting and sitting closer are clues that he cannot see clearly, so board means the classroom board where the teacher writes. «If you cannot see the board at school, tell a teacher and a parent.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Old card and board games from grandparents' childhoods are still fun to play today» means a flat piece for a game, like a chess board. Does your meaning still make sense? If yes, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Board can be a noun or a verb. As a noun it is a flat surface or a flat piece. As a verb, to board means to get on a bus, train, plane or ship.
fact: A board in class is a flat surface where the teacher writes, such as a whiteboard or blackboard.
fact: A board can be a flat piece of wood, like a skateboard or a surfboard.
fact: A board for a game is a flat piece where players move their pieces, such as a chess board.
fact: «On board» means on a bus, train, plane or ship. «Board the train» means get on the train.
exercise: «If you cannot see the board at school, tell a teacher and a parent.» What is the board in this sentence? | *A flat surface in class where the teacher writes | A flat piece for a game | A long flat piece of wood for building | To get on a bus
exercise: Lily says, «We will board the train at nine o'clock.» What does board mean here? | To write on the train | To play a game | A flat piece of wood | *To get on the train
exercise: «White has taken 5 pieces and Black 3: 32 − 5 − 3 = 24 pieces are still on the board.» What is the board in this sentence? | A long piece of wood | A bus or a train | *A flat piece for a game, like a chess board | A notice on the wall
test: «Old card and board games from grandparents' childhoods are still fun to play today.» In this sentence, what does board mean? | To get on a ship | A flat surface for writing on | *A flat piece for a game | A plank of wood for building
test: Dad says, «We will board the plane at gate 5.» What does board mean? | A flat piece for a game | A long flat piece of wood | To write on the plane | *To get on the plane
exam: Sam read a notice on the notice board, then rode his skateboard to the park. In «skateboard», what does board mean? | *A flat piece of wood to stand on | A flat surface in class where the teacher writes | To get on a bus | A piece for a game
